--
--
C++17 aggregate initialization with a base-class element (N5008
[dcl.init.aggr]/2.2): `derived{{}, 7}` in a RETURN expression, where
derived's base is an EMPTY class template instance (the libc++
__take_closure/__range_adaptor_closure shape).  The leading {} clause
initializes the base element; previously it was paired with the first
data member and the enclosing body was silently dropped.
